"Artemis Base Camp Principle #04": "Astronaut Tip",
"Even when everything appears completely normal, lunar astronauts constantly monitor their habitat, closed-loop life support (ECLSS), and power arrays. Regular routine checks help identify problems early before minor drifts affect crew safety.": "Even when everything looks fine, astronauts keep checking their base, their air and water machines, and their solar panels. Checking often helps you find small problems before they grow.",
"All primary and backup base systems are currently operating at peak engineered condition with zero anomalies.": "All the base machines, and the spare ones too, are working perfectly. Nothing is wrong.",
"Space habitats have no atmosphere outside, so constant ECLSS situational awareness ensures life support redundancy is never taken for granted.": "There is no air outside a space base, so astronauts always keep watching their air machines and never take them for granted.",
"CONTINUE MISSION & PROCEED TO EVALUATION": "CONTINUE THE MISSION",
