"STEM Curricular Module": "Learn More",
"NASA Science Classroom — Lunar Dust & Solar Energy": "Science Class: Moon Dust and Solar Power",
"Solar panels convert sunlight into clean electricity using photovoltaic cells. On Earth, wind and rain wash dust away. But on the Moon, there is no weather! Lunar regolith dust is jagged, razor-sharp, and holds an electrostatic charge from direct solar radiation, causing it to cling tightly to glass solar panels.": "Solar panels turn sunlight into electricity. On Earth, wind and rain wash the dust off. But the Moon has no weather! Moon dust is sharp, and sunlight makes it sticky, so it clings to the panels.",
"What Happened? Regolith dust settled on Arrays Alpha & Beta.": "What happened? Moon dust landed on Panels A and B.",
"Why Does It Matter? Keeping panels clean produces the kilowatt power needed for crew science and experiments.": "Why does it matter? Clean panels make the power the crew needs for science.",
"Lunar Dust Shielding Tech": "Dust Shield Invention",
"NASA researchers design electrodynamic dust shields (EDS) that use invisible electric waves to push dust right off solar glass!": "NASA scientists are making special panels that use invisible electric waves to push dust right off!",
"SIMULATED MISSION • NASA SPACE APPS": "SIMULATED MISSION • NASA SPACE APPS",
"17. Solar Particle Event — Shelter Now!": "Solar Storm: Get to the Shelter!",
"Scientists record solar flares every day in NASA's DONKI database. A strong X-class flare is the kind of event this mission practises for.": "Scientists write down every solar flare in a NASA database called DONKI. A very strong flare, called an X-class flare, is what this mission helps you get ready for.",
