"Artemis Base Storm Shelter Status": "Storm Shelter",
"Multilayer Regolith + Water Wall Buffer Active": "Moon soil and water walls are protecting us",
"3. ECLSS Oxygen Loop Safe": "3. The air machine is working",
"Radiation Absorption Rate: 99.4% Blocked": "Harmful rays blocked: almost all",
"The Sun constantly radiates light and warmth, but during intense coronal mass ejections and solar flares, it fires energetic atomic particles (mostly protons) across space at nearly the speed of light!": "The Sun always gives us light and warmth. But sometimes it has a solar flare or a giant burst, and it shoots tiny fast particles into space, almost as fast as light!",
"Earth vs. Moon Protection: On Earth, our strong global magnetic field and thick atmosphere deflect almost all solar storm particles. But the Moon has no global magnetic shield or air—so lunar astronauts use lunar regolith (compacted moon dirt) and water wall jackets in habitats as shields!": "Earth is protected by its thick air and a magnetic shield. The Moon has neither. So Moon astronauts use thick Moon soil and walls of water as shields!",
