"Screen 23: Breathe Easy! (ECLSS)": "Quest 1: Breathe Easy!",
"HABITAT LIFE SUPPORT (ECLSS)": "LIFE SUPPORT",
"Space has zero air and zero atmospheric pressure! Inside our lunar outpost, specialized machines work every second to clean our air, provide fresh oxygen, and recycle every single drop of water.": "Space has no air at all! Inside our Moon base, special machines work every second. They clean the air, make fresh oxygen, and reuse every drop of water.",
"Target Standard: 101.3 kPa Sea-Level Mix": "Air pressure kept the same as on Earth: 101.3 kPa",
"LUNAR EXPEDITION CHIEF SCIENCE OFFICER": "CHIEF SCIENTIST",
"\"Welcome to the Life Support Laboratory, Cadet! On the Moon, we cannot simply open a window for fresh air. Let's discover how our habitat helps astronauts breathe and stay comfortable!\"": "\"Welcome to the Life Support Lab, Cadet! On the Moon, we cannot just open a window for fresh air. Let's find out how our base helps astronauts breathe!\"",
"Welcome to the Life Support Laboratory, Cadet! On the Moon, we cannot simply open a window for fresh air. Let's discover how our habitat helps astronauts breathe and stay comfortable!": "Welcome to the Life Support Lab, Cadet! On the Moon, we cannot just open a window for fresh air. Let's find out how our base helps astronauts breathe!",
"ECLSS Mission Modules": "4 Life Support Jobs",
"Explore the four primary systems sustaining life inside a sealed space habitat.": "Explore the four jobs that keep people alive inside a space base.",
"MODULE 01": "JOB 1",
"Without gravity-driven thermal air convection, exhaled carbon dioxide would pool around sleeping astronauts like an invisible bubble. Continuous fans circulate fresh oxygen throughout every corridor.": "In space, the air you breathe out does not float away. It can make a bubble around a sleeping astronaut! Fans keep fresh air moving everywhere.",
"MODULE 02": "JOB 2",
"Remove Carbon Dioxide": "Remove Carbon Dioxide",
"Humans breathe in oxygen and exhale CO2. Advanced regenerative scrubbers and amine filters trap and vent excess CO2 before it can cause headaches or oxygen depletion.": "We breathe in oxygen and breathe out carbon dioxide (CO2). Special filters catch the CO2 before it can give you a headache.",
"Scrubber: CDRA Active": "CO2 filter: working",
"MODULE 03": "JOB 3",
"Water is super heavy to launch from Earth! Lunar life support captures cabin humidity from breath and sweat, distilling it with urine processor assemblies into ultrapure drinking water.": "Water is very heavy to send from Earth! So the base collects water from our breath and sweat and cleans it until it is safe to drink.",
"MODULE 04": "JOB 4",
"Monitor the Habitat": "Watch the Base",
"Dozens of sensors constantly watch habitat air pressure (held at 101.3 kPa like Earth's beaches), track O2 partial pressure, and balance thermal radiators against the -130°C to +120°C lunar surface swings.": "Lots of sensors watch the air pressure, keep it like the seaside on Earth, and keep the base at a nice temperature even when it is boiling or freezing outside.",
"Atmosphere: 101.3 kPa": "Air pressure: 101.3 kPa",
"Nominal ➔": "Normal ➔",
"HANDS-ON SIMULATION LAB": "TRY IT YOURSELF",
"Connect each ECLSS subsystem on the left to its critical biological mission on the right. Tap cards to form pairs!": "Match each machine on the left to its job on the right. Tap two cards to make a pair!",
"Carbon dioxide removal": "Removes carbon dioxide",
"Amine Scrubber Unit": "CO2 Filter",
"Atmosphere Telemetry": "Air Sensors",
"2. Habitat Function": "2. What it does",
"Cleans cabin atmosphere": "Cleans the air",
"Checks habitat pressure and temperature": "Checks the air pressure and temperature",
"Select a Life Support Subsystem, then select its matching Habitat Function!": "Pick a machine, then pick what it does!",
"What happens when astronauts breathe out carbon dioxide in a closed habitat?": "What happens when astronauts breathe out carbon dioxide inside a space base?",
"Think about why an airtight room on the Moon is different from walking around outside on Earth.": "Think: a sealed room on the Moon is not like being outside on Earth.",
"Life-support scrubbers remove it from the cabin air.": "Filters take it out of the air.",
"\"Spacecraft and habitats need carefully managed life-support systems because astronauts cannot rely on Earth's open environment.\"": "\"Space bases need life support machines because astronauts cannot use Earth's open air.\"",
"Spacecraft and habitats need carefully managed life-support systems because astronauts cannot rely on Earth's open environment.": "Space bases need life support machines because astronauts cannot use Earth's open air.",
"On Earth, vast forests, blue oceans, and a huge atmosphere naturally recycle carbon dioxide back into oxygen and filter fresh rainwater. On the Moon, our entire planetary biosphere is engineered inside compact titanium boxes!": "On Earth, forests, oceans and air clean the air for us. On the Moon, people need machines inside the base to do the same job!",
"Earth Biosphere vs. Closed Lunar ECLSS Loop": "Earth cleans its air by itself. A Moon base needs machines.",
"Golden oxygen molecule emblem awarded for mastering closed-loop habitat life support.": "A golden oxygen badge for learning about life support.",
