"24. Solar Storm Alert! — Understanding Space Radiation": "Quest 2: Solar Storm Alert!",
"Space radiation is one of the most critical challenges for human lunar exploration. Discover how solar weather behaves and how lunar astronauts protect themselves.": "Space radiation is one of the biggest dangers for astronauts on the Moon. Find out about space weather and how astronauts stay safe.",
"“Cadet, the Sun is more than a bright light! It can release energetic particles into space. Let's discover why astronauts need to understand space radiation.”": "“Cadet, the Sun is more than a bright light! It can shoot tiny fast particles into space. Let's find out why astronauts need to know about space radiation.”",
"Cadet, the Sun is more than a bright light! It can release energetic particles into space. Let's discover why astronauts need to understand space radiation.": "Cadet, the Sun is more than a bright light! It can shoot tiny fast particles into space. Let's find out why astronauts need to know about space radiation.",
"SAFETY PROTOCOL INITIATED": "SAFETY FIRST",
"Lunar Science Modules": "4 Things to Learn",
"MODULE A": "PART A",
"Coronal mass ejections and energetic protons travel across space at millions of miles per hour, creating dynamic space weather events that reach the Moon.": "Sometimes the Sun throws out giant bursts of tiny particles. They travel through space at millions of miles an hour and can reach the Moon. This is called space weather.",
"MODULE B": "PART B",
"Unlike on Earth, the Moon has no atmosphere or global magnetic field. Invisible high-energy particles traverse space freely, requiring artificial protection.": "Earth has thick air and a magnetic shield. The Moon has neither. So invisible space particles reach the ground, and astronauts need their own shields.",
"MODULE C": "PART C",
"Astronauts stay safe using 3+ meters of lunar regolith soil piled over underground modules, water-filled barrier walls, and multi-layered spacesuits.": "Astronauts stay safe with more than 3 metres of Moon soil piled on their base, walls filled with water, and space suits with many layers.",
"Regolith & Water Walls": "Moon Soil and Water Walls",
"MODULE D": "PART D",
"Compact dosimeters on suits and orbital satellites give early warnings. Crews quickly halt extravehicular moonwalks and retreat into fortified shelters.": "Small radiation meters on suits and satellites in space give an early warning. When the alert sounds, crews stop their moonwalk and hurry into the shelter.",
"Tap the correct action protocol that matches each lunar space weather phenomenon.": "Match each Moon space weather word to the right idea.",
"Helps astronauts track exposure conditions": "Shows how much radiation astronauts get",
"Regolith Shielding": "Moon Soil Shield",
