"Because a lunar night lasts roughly 14 Earth days (336 hours!), lunar bases can't rely solely on solar panels. A continuous source like Fission Surface Power and battery buffers keeps life support alive!": "The Moon night lasts about 14 Earth days (336 hours!), so a base cannot rely only on solar panels. Batteries and a nuclear power machine keep the air machines running!",
