"Remember: the Moon's nights last 14 Earth days in total darkness. Review the modules above and try option A!": "Remember: the Moon night lasts 14 Earth days and it is totally dark. Read the parts above and try answer A!",
"GRID ONLINE: FULL DUAL-POWER ENGAGED!": "POWER ON! Solar and back-up power are connected!",
"LED Grow Spectrum Active": "Plant lights are on",
"Red and deep blue wavelengths pulsing at 300 µmol/m²/s to accelerate photosynthesis.": "Red and blue light helps plants make their food faster.",
"SPECTRUM TUNED (RED/BLUE)": "LIGHT SET (RED AND BLUE)",
"Capillary Hydration Delivered": "Water delivered",
"50ml nutrient elixir injected directly into the seed envelope! Water hugs roots in 1/6 gravity.": "Water and plant food went into the seed pillow. The water stays close to the roots!",
"NUTRIENTS & WATER BALANCED": "WATER AND PLANT FOOD READY",
"Success! Bountiful lunar microgreens and dwarf space tomatoes ready for crew nutrition!": "Success! Fresh baby plants and tiny tomatoes are ready for the crew to eat!",
"OPTIMAL HARVEST REACHED!": "HARVEST TIME!",
"NASA grows plants aboard spacecraft and lunar bases to provide fresh vitamins (A, C, K) that degrade in packaged meals, as well as to study cellular responses to microgravity and boost astronaut morale.": "NASA grows plants in space to give astronauts fresh vitamins that packed food can lose. Plants also make astronauts feel happy, and scientists learn how plants grow without gravity.",
"Remember: while space is wild, plants are grown primarily for astronaut nutrition, psychological well-being, and scientific biology research!": "Remember: we grow plants in space for food, to feel happy, and to learn about plants!",
"PROCESSING LUNAR REGOLITH: Heating to 900°C in carbothermal reactor... Liberated 42% O2 gas! Sintered residue molded into habitat building block!": "MOON SOIL: A very hot oven makes oxygen gas come out! The leftover soil can be pressed into building bricks!",
"PROCESSING ANORTHOSITE ROCKS: Crushed with high-impact sonic pulverizer. Titanium extracted for rover chassis; silicon wafers synthesized!": "SPECIAL ROCKS: Crushing them gives us metal for the rover and silicon for solar panels!",
"PROCESSING WATER ICE CORES: Thermal sublimation chamber engaged! Pure H2O filtered for drinking; Electrolysis separating liquid H2 and LOX rocket propellants!": "ICE: Melted and cleaned, it gives us water to drink. Electricity can split it to make rocket fuel too!",
"HARVESTING CRATER RIM SOLAR RAYS: Photovoltaic array tracking continuous 360° solar incidence at 285 W/m²! Power reserves refreshed to 100%!": "MOUNTAIN TOP SUNLIGHT: The Sun shines here almost all the time, so solar panels make power day and night!",
"Correct! ISRU stands for In-Situ Resource Utilization — discovering, harvesting, and transforming natural lunar materials into life-saving oxygen, clean water, and deep-space rocket fuel!": "Correct! ISRU means using what you find on the Moon, like turning Moon materials into oxygen, water and rocket fuel!",
"Not quite! Remember: Option A is correct. ISRU means \"living off the land\" by utilizing in-place local lunar minerals, rocks, and ice deposits!": "Not quite! Answer A is right. ISRU means using the rocks, soil and ice that are already on the Moon!",
